{"title":"2004 AIME I Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle\" title=\"Triangle\">triangle</a> with sides 3, 4, and 5, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c16df895dad08efcc67a9a5d66f8eb08a7c37e8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DEFG$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> be a 6-by-7 <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rectangle\" title=\"Rectangle\">rectangle</a>. A segment is drawn to divide triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> into a triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/b/3cb141913b3ab1abe79fb14c5b39a9568faa5543.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> and a trapezoid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/f/72f539a3dc0cea9899543319d030a34ca6c33b0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> and another segment is drawn to divide rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c16df895dad08efcc67a9a5d66f8eb08a7c37e8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DEFG$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> into a triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/b/87b484c85151278e0b91832124fc1e67f2dd2e92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> and a trapezoid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/2/ec2fe4ffdca06f7e4f7e2df05465a894eda12eb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/b/3cb141913b3ab1abe79fb14c5b39a9568faa5543.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> is similar to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/b/87b484c85151278e0b91832124fc1e67f2dd2e92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/f/72f539a3dc0cea9899543319d030a34ca6c33b0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> is similar to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/6/2c6cc788b59d23384adc1b6b733ce8a86f70ed3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V_2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> The minimum value of the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/b/3cb141913b3ab1abe79fb14c5b39a9568faa5543.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> can be written in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/1/271cdd78c4c10cde94410584ce7282874413cb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m/n,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Relatively_prime\" title=\"Relatively prime\">relatively prime</a> positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5db26f75f6218a382840f0ed34f5d36bcff61d33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/5/045ea623c72f6feb8466866624df6eddc9dd83c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=3, AC=4, DE=6, DG=7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"273\" height=\"16\" /> for the purpose of labeling. Clearly, the dividing segment in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c16df895dad08efcc67a9a5d66f8eb08a7c37e8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DEFG$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> must go through one of its vertices, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Without_loss_of_generality\" title=\"Without loss of generality\">without loss of generality</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. The other endpoint (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/3/b239e47c75fa1adfb0e7d7fb6bf219fcc53f86d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D&#39;$\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" />) of the segment can either lie on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/0/ed0f6a692f19a65fe60fe5745826792f3fd1d57e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{EF}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/4/8f450f6af9c000449bff7dc1801fdd77978f6e24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{FG}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/2/ec2fe4ffdca06f7e4f7e2df05465a894eda12eb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> is a trapezoid with a right angle then, from which it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/f/72f539a3dc0cea9899543319d030a34ca6c33b0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> contains one of the right angles of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/b/3cb141913b3ab1abe79fb14c5b39a9568faa5543.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> is similar to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/b/3cb141913b3ab1abe79fb14c5b39a9568faa5543.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" />, and hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/b/87b484c85151278e0b91832124fc1e67f2dd2e92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" />, are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/9/d394f31aa3a29ae941a008a03dbb31e8e78a0282.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3-4-5\\,\\triangle$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"90\" height=\"14\" />s.  \n</p><p>Suppose we find the ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> of the smaller base to the larger base for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/2/ec2fe4ffdca06f7e4f7e2df05465a894eda12eb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />, which consequently is the same ratio for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/f/72f539a3dc0cea9899543319d030a34ca6c33b0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />. By similar triangles, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/3/a831b33003033f5afaa11655e74e52c9d1cc0293.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U_1 \\sim \\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"18\" /> by the same ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, and since the ratio of the areas of two similar figures is equal to the square of the ratio of their corresponding lengths, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/c/e8c9a2bb2d1b4f4f039e1ad624fb5c216a6e83e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[U_1] = r^2 \\cdot [ABC] = 6r^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"184\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p>\n<center><table><tbody><tr><td>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/e/95e4c2b2b26503d8b7fa02636a0c6b5354f8a509.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] defaultpen(linewidth(0.7));  pair A=(0,0),B=(0,3),C=(4,0); draw(MP(&quot;A&quot;,A)--MP(&quot;B&quot;,B,N)--MP(&quot;C&quot;,C)--cycle); draw((9*4/14,0)--(9*4/14,5*3/14),dashed); label(&quot;\\(V_1\\)&quot;,(1,1.2)); label(&quot;\\(U_1\\)&quot;,(3,0.3)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"215\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/d/38d98d7d3f19fa53824b61f1f011b3f6ab248b26.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] defaultpen(linewidth(0.7)); pointpen = black; pair D=(0,0),E=(0,6),F=(7,6),G=(7,0),H=(4.5,6); draw(MP(&quot;D&quot;,D)--MP(&quot;E&quot;,E,N)--MP(&quot;F&quot;,F,N)--MP(&quot;G&quot;,G)--cycle); draw(D--D(MP(&quot;D&#39;&quot;,H,N)),dashed); label(&quot;\\(U_2\\)&quot;,(1,3)); label(&quot;\\(V_2\\)&quot;,(5,3)); MP(&quot;7&quot;,(D+G)/2,S); MP(&quot;6&quot;,(D+E)/2,W); MP(&quot;9/2&quot;,(E+H)/2,N); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"238\" />\n</p>\n</td></tr><tr><td>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/f/e3f4ede63658070fbff16cca8f5353f7d5561902.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] defaultpen(linewidth(0.7));  pair A=(0,0),B=(0,3),C=(4,0); draw(MP(&quot;A&quot;,A)--MP(&quot;B&quot;,B,N)--MP(&quot;C&quot;,C)--cycle); draw((3.5,0)--(3.5,3/8),dashed); label(&quot;\\(V_1\\)&quot;,(1.5,1)); label(&quot;\\(U_1\\)&quot;,(3.8,0.4)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"215\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/3/c035564e49401be97ad133f29406e5eebb12a26a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] defaultpen(linewidth(0.7));  pointpen = black; pair D=(0,0),E=(0,6),F=(7,6),G=(7,0),H=(7,21/4); draw(MP(&quot;D&quot;,D)--MP(&quot;E&quot;,E,N)--MP(&quot;F&quot;,F,N)--MP(&quot;G&quot;,G)--cycle); draw(D--D(MP(&quot;D&#39;&quot;,H,NW)),dashed); label(&quot;\\(V_2\\)&quot;,(2,3)); label(&quot;\\(U_2\\)&quot;,(5,1)); MP(&quot;7&quot;,(D+G)/2,S); MP(&quot;6&quot;,(D+E)/2,W); MP(&quot;21/4&quot;,(G+H)/2,(-1,0)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"235\" />\n</p>\n</td></tr></tbody></table></center>\n<ul><li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/3/b239e47c75fa1adfb0e7d7fb6bf219fcc53f86d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D&#39;$\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> lies on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/0/ed0f6a692f19a65fe60fe5745826792f3fd1d57e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{EF}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9ff94aa1f33d66c9d79e88ca4d008ce3ee8a638.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ED&#39; = \\frac34 \\cdot 6 = \\frac{9}{2},\\, 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"154\" height=\"38\" /> from maintaining the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/1/af1a2cb4ff1720f169ddde1726c1a5a1ab816ae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3-4-5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" /> triangular ratio; the latter (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/7/d07fb7271ceb2c826682c811bca8ca53381cd91a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac43 \\cdot 6 = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"70\" height=\"38\" />) can be discarded as extraneous since we need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/1/c01019873b7f4e6e5d9c52ae7229f7ff2204193d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ED&#39;&lt;EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"89\" height=\"17\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/d/70d685552a265ce44952902f32a9b75ff63d24de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D&#39;F = \\frac{5}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"70\" height=\"37\" />, and the ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/1/d81922590deca5055afe8b2f729519b95108d991.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\frac{D&#39;F}{DG} = \\frac{5}{14}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"116\" height=\"38\" />. The area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/6/b16b7c4d54547aa30780ee2c43e178b6131ea71f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[U_1] = 6\\left(\\frac{5}{14}\\right)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"120\" height=\"46\" /> in this case.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/3/b239e47c75fa1adfb0e7d7fb6bf219fcc53f86d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D&#39;$\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> lies on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/4/8f450f6af9c000449bff7dc1801fdd77978f6e24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{FG}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/a/01ae7428076f0a7b45c485a2ffabd1179f606c6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GD&#39; = \\frac{21}{4},\\, \\frac{28}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"112\" height=\"38\" />; the latter can be discarded as extraneous since we need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/f/e8f1ec5920fa3865e516b292db9cb5f6232abce7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GD&#39;&lt;GF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"89\" height=\"17\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/0/f1043dbca806190ce537324131308d7116a71bda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D&#39;F = \\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"70\" height=\"38\" />, and the ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/3/2a362774fd4c92ae888aa4547a24a79f5b418305.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\frac{D&#39;F}{DE} = \\frac{1}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"107\" height=\"38\" />. The area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/e/86e9acda96a047d48ae880825e0fdf4e5a6213ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[U_1] = 6\\left(\\frac{1}{8}\\right)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"111\" height=\"46\" /> in this case.</li></ul>\n<p>Of the two cases, the second is smaller; the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/e/3ee66c9325b562140f40a1fe274aae1900873d8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{32}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/5/075b5cfb4245ffa769849b57d5efe48f7efb3ae6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n = \\boxed{035}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://youtu.be/HH381svVs_E?si=Y6B51-pl_1LG5Lk_\">2004 AIME I #9</a>\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://mathproblemsolvingskills.wordpress.com/\">MathProblemSolvingSkills.com</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I\" title=\"2004 AIME I\">2004 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2004 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2004 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2004\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Probl